Thought: I'll use batch_retrieve_polymorphs with a list of common nitride compositions. I'll include both binary and ternary nitrides to ensure diversity.
Action: batch_retrieve_polymorphs
Action Input: {"compositions": ["AlN", "GaN", "InN", "BN", "TiN", "ZrN", "HfN", "VN", "NbN", "TaN", "CrN", "MoN", "WN", "ScN", "YN", "LaN", "Si3N4", "Ge3N4", "Sn3N4", "Ca3N2", "Sr3N2", "Ba3N2", "Mg3N2", "Li3N", "Na3N", "K3N", "Be3N2", "Zn3N2", "Cd3N2", "AlGaN", "InGaN", "TiZrN", "HfTaN", "VNbN", "CrMoN", "ScYN", "LiCaN", "MgZnN", "SiGeN"], "max_energy_above_hull": 0.3, "max_per_composition": 3, "save_directory": "polymorph_data"}

